.TH APPLE-DEVICES 1 "2026-10-28" "apple-devices 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
apple-devices \- manage Apple devices over USB
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B apple-devices
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B apple-devices
is a GTK4/libadwaita application for managing Apple devices (iPhone, iPad,
iPod touch) connected over USB. It talks to the device through the open
libimobiledevice stack (usbmuxd/lockdownd/AFC).
.PP
The Music section browses the on-device media library, imports audio files
together with their embedded cover art (covers become visible in the
device Music app immediately), exports and deletes tracks. A backup of the
device media library database is taken before every write.
.SH OPTIONS
This program follows the usual GNU command line syntax. See
.B "apple-devices --help"
for a summary of options.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/apple-devices/settings.ini
Application settings (interface language and similar).
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/apple-devices/backups/
Automatic backups of the device media library database, one per write.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR usbmuxd (8),
.BR ideviceinfo (1),
.BR ifuse (1)
